    "text": {
     "en": "Traditional farming uses bullocks, simple ploughs and manual work. Modern farming uses tractors, improved seeds, fertilisers and drip or sprinkler irrigation.\nFarmers face challenges such as irregular rain, pests, debt, rising costs and low prices.\nOrganic farming avoids chemicals. Crop rotation and mixed cropping keep the soil fertile."
    }
